        <owl:annotatedTarget>The common lymphoid progenitor (CLP) arises from the multipotential hematopoietic stem cell in the bone marrow. Hematopoietic stem cells have the unique capability of developing into any type of blood cell depending on the body&apos;s requirements. In contrast, common lymphoid progenitors are already committed to the lymphoid lineage but are still oligopotent with the capability to further differentiate into various types of lymphoid cells. 
