        <owl:annotatedTarget>Oenocytes are highly variable in size, shape, cluster formation and anatomical location. In adults, oenocytes tend to be smaller but more numerous than in larvae. While oenocytes have been found in arachnids and crustaceans, they have been most abundantly described in insects.</owl:annotatedTarget>
