        <owl:annotatedTarget>The CD8-alpha alpha positive, gamma-delta intraepithelial T cell are a subset of intraepithelial lymphocytes (IELs), a highly heterogeneous population of immune cell that resides within the epithelial layer of mucosal barriers. CD8-alpha alpha positive, gamma-delta intraepithelial T cell are predominantly found in the gastrointestinal tract. They are characterized by the expression of both CD8-alpha-alpha homodimer and the gamma-delta (γδ) variant of the T cell receptor (TCR). CD8-alpha alpha positive, gamma-delta are thought to represent the most typical γδ IEL subset in the intestine.
