        <obo:IAO_0000115>An immature myeloid leukocyte of heterogeneous phenotype found particularly in cancer and sepsis patients that is capable of suppressing activity of T cells in ex vivo assays. This cell type is CD45-positive, CD11b-positive.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl#blood_and_immune_upper_slim"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl#cellxgene_subset"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Markers: Mouse: CD11b+GR1+CD31+; Human: CD34+ CD33+CD15-CD13+. (According to some reports in humans these cells are iNOS+ARG1+IL13+IFNg+); location: In cancerous tissue; in the blood and lymphoid organs in sepsis.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>myeloid suppressor cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
