        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fully differentiated plasma cell that lives for years, as opposed to months, secretes immunoglobulin, and has the phenotype weakly CD19-positive, CD20-negative, CD38-negative, strongly CD138-positive, MHC Class II-negative, surface immunoglobulin-negative, IgD-negative, and strongly CXCR4-positive. The majority of these cells of this type reside in the bone marrow.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>long lived plasma cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
