        <owl:annotatedTarget>A preadipocyte is an immature precursor to adipocytes, which are specialized cells primarily tasked with the storage of energy in the form of lipids, making them key in metabolic regulation and overall energy homeostasis. Preadipocytes are present in the stromal vascular fraction of adipose tissues and can be identified by their fibroblastic morphology and the expression of specific markers such as Pref-1, CD24, CD34, and CD29.
