        <owl:annotatedTarget>A large nucleated basophilic erythrocyte found in mammalian embryos. This cell type arises from the blood islands of yolk sacs and expresses different types of hemoglobins (beta-H1, gamma-1 and zeta) than adult erythrocytes. Considered a type of erythroblast as this cell type can enucleate in circulation.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DOI:10.1097/MOH.0b013e3282f97ae1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
