        <obo:IAO_0000115>A myeloid dendritic cell found in the blood that is CD16-positive.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>CD16+ mDC</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>CD16-mDC</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Normally represent 65-75% of peripheral blood mDCs (human). They are also CD281-positive (TLR1), CD282-positive (TLR2), CD284-positive (TLR4), CD285-positive (TLR5), CD286-positive (TLR6), CD288-positive (TLR8), CD289-positive (TLR9), and CD290-positive (TLR10) by RT-PCR [PMID:17332250]. Upon TLR stimulation, these cells are potent producers of TNF-alpha, while producing little CXCL8 (IL8).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>CD16-positive myeloid dendritic cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
