        <obo:IAO_0000115>A mesangial cell located among the glomerular capillaries in a renal corpuscle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>KUPO:0001032</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>intraglomerular mesangial cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl#cellxgene_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#human_reference_atlas"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Like smooth muscle, a glomerular mesangial cell is contractile and possesses the filaments actin and myosin. The contractile mechanism is also similar to that of smooth muscle, with Ca2+/calmodulin-activated myosin light-chain kinase instigating myosin-actin cross-bridge cycling. Mesangial cell phagocytosis of apoptotic neutrophils involves a novel CD36-independent, alpha(v)beta3/TSP-mediated mechanism that is uncoupled from chemokine secretion, emphasizing the injury-limiting potential of mesangial cell phagocytosis of apoptotic cells.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>glomerular mesangial cell</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:depiction>https://cdn.humanatlas.io/digital-objects/2d-ftu/kidney-renal-corpuscle/v1.2/assets/2d-ftu-kidney-renal-corpuscle.png</foaf:depiction>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
