        <obo:IAO_0000115>An epithelial cell part of respiratory tract epithelium that is a precursor of a multi-ciliated cell. This cell actively amplifies centrioles, a required step for multiciliogenesis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489"/>
        <terms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9185-3994"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2023-06-20T10:27:17Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl#added_by_HRA"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl#cellxgene_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#human_reference_atlas"/>
        <rdfs:comment>In humans, deuterosomal cells have been noted to have enriched expression of the following: PLK4, FOXJ1, DEUP1, FOXN4, YPEL1, HES6 and CDC20B. Deuterosomal cells were termed after deuterosomes, the platforms of active centriole amplification.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>deuterosomal cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
